Only "Completed route hides active todos" fails when run after "Main and footer shown". The other routing scenarios pass.

The "Completed route" scenario expects that after navigating to `#/completed`, the active todo "Active task" is NOT visible (display: none). But it IS visible (display: flex).

This means the filtering isn't working correctly for `#/completed`. Let me check: does `getVisibleTodos()` return only completed todos when hash is `#/completed`?

The function:
```javascript
function getVisibleTodos() {    var hash = window.location.hash || '#/';


```

Checking the filtering logic...

The function checks the hash and returns only completed todos when navigating to `#/completed`, or all todos by default. So when the hash is `#/completed`, it should filter out the active todo "Active task" and only show completed ones. The test is verifying this filtering behavior works correctly.

Now I'm looking at the `navigate` method to see how it handles hash changes. It sets the location hash and dispatches a hashchange event, which should trigger the filter to update. But there might be a timing issue or the event listener isn't firing properly when the hash is set.

```

javascript
navigate(hash) {
    if (!this.window) throw new Error('...');
    if (this.window.location.hash === hash) return;
    this.window.location.hash = hash;
    this.window.dispatchEvent(new this.window.Event('hashchange'));
}
```

